@flexiarg buffer-cleaner/classify-staleness
@title Classify Staleness
@keywords classify, prior, needed-later, uncertainty, age, file-stale
@audience adapter, G computation
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade technique
@references [buffer-cleaner/observe-categories buffer-cleaner/kill]
@provenance v3 diagram chip 2; the genuinely-uncertain channel. Live evaluation: futon2 buffer-cleaner-adapter (src/buffer_cleaner/classify.clj); parameter values below are the DECLARATION — all :constructed (futon2 a508aa24/74c298f0); the real cleaner cannot measure revisit rates.

! conclusion:
  Each candidate is classified {decisiveness, prior-needed-later,
  revisit-cost} from the category table and, for file-stale, from the
  age->prior map; :file-stale is resolved from age + the wiring's
  threshold.

  + PARAMETER-TABLE (the declaration; the lab's categories.edn is its
    machine projection):
    stream  :decisive   p=0.0* cost 1.0   (*fixture premise, not attested)
    http    :decisive   p=0.0* cost 1.0   (*fixture premise, not attested)
    temp    :uncertain  p=0.05 cost 1.0   (process-gone makes the kill
                                           mechanism safe, not the future)
    dired   :uncertain  p=0.25 cost 0.5
    render  :uncertain  p=0.10 cost 1.0
    invoke  :uncertain  p=0.20 cost 2.0
    file-stale :uncertain cost 5.0, prior by age: {21600s 0.40,
                86400s 0.05, default 0.05} — a stale-age threshold
                ENCODES a prior over needed-later; we declare it.

  + HOWEVER: no age histogram can infer revisit probabilities; these
    remain constructed conditional assumptions, labeled as such into G.
